+++ b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-11-add-task-timestamps/design.md
@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+## Context
+
+`src/domain/` must not read the clock, so timestamps cannot be made there. Tasks are built by `createTask` and changed by pure functions in `task.ts`, orchestrated by `createTaskList` in `list.ts`. The public entry is `createTodoList` in `src/index.ts`.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:**
+- Timestamps on every task, deterministic under test.
+
+**Non-Goals:**
+- Displaying ages, sorting by time, persistence.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- A `Clock` is a function returning an ISO-8601 string. `createTaskList(now)` takes it; task functions (`createTask`, `completeTask`, `reopenTask`, `renameTask`, `addTag`, `removeTag`) take the time as a parameter.
+- `createTodoList(now = () => new Date().toISOString())` in `src/index.ts`, outside the domain, supplies the real clock; tests pass a fake one.
+- The list reads the clock once per operation, only after the operation is known to succeed, so failures leave `updatedAt` untouched.
+- A successful `tag` of an already-present tag, or `untag` of an absent one, still sets `updatedAt` (the call succeeded; keeping it simple and uniform).
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- Tasks now include two more fields, so callers deep-comparing tasks must adapt.
