@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+## Why
+
+The app should show how old a task is and what changed recently, so the list must record when each task was created and last changed.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Every task gets `createdAt` and `updatedAt`, ISO-8601 date-time strings.
+- On `add` the two are equal.
+- Every successful change to a task (complete, reopen, rename, tag, untag) sets `updatedAt` to the time of the change; `createdAt` never changes.
+- The list takes its time from a clock supplied at its edge, so the domain code does not read the wall clock.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+- `task-list`: tasks carry creation and last-change timestamps.
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/domain/task.ts`, `src/domain/list.ts`, `src/index.ts`, `test/list.test.ts`.
+- `Task` gains two fields, so code comparing whole tasks sees them. No new dependency.
